(oregano) as needed
(rosemary) as needed
(potato, optional) as desired
(yoghurt, optional, for serving) as desired
(bread, fresh, optional, for serving) as desired
# Method-only items
(olive oil) some
(salt) as needed
(pepper) as needed
(water) 1 cup; more if needed

::equipment

(pot, lidded, oven-safe) -OR- (roasting tray, sided, foil cover)
(oven)
(refrigerator)

::instructions

# Night before
{marinade} = (olive oil) + (lemon: juice) of half a lemon + (oregano) + (rosemary) + (salt) + (pepper)
{marinade} <mix>
(lamb) + {marinade} <rub>
    <marinate, refrigerator, overnight>
# Next day
(oven) <heat, 375f / 190c / gas mark 5>
(garlic) <separate, cloves, leave skin or peel as preferred>
(carrot) + (leek) + (onion) + (lemon) remaining <chop, chunks>
Optional [
    (potato) <chop, chunks>
]
{lamb pot} = (lamb) + (garlic) + (carrot) + (leek) + (onion) + (lemon) remaining
{lamb pot} <arrange, vegetables underneath and around meat, lidded oven-safe pot or sided roasting tray tightly sealed with foil>
Optional [
    {lamb pot} + (potato)
]
{lamb pot} + {marinade} juices + (water) 1 cup
    <cook, oven, 2 1/2-3h, check halfway and add water if needed to prevent burning>
Optional [
    {lamb pot} <uncover>
        <brown, a few minutes if needed>
]
(lamb) <pull apart>
    <serve, optional yoghurt and bread; juices may be gravy>

::story

You'll need a good-sized lidded pot that can go in the oven for this. But if you don't have that then you can use a large roasting tray with sides and cover it with foil, sealing it as best you can. It's an excellent celebration or Sunday meal.

